  "Number": 1,
  "Question": "Compute the sum of all the roots of \\[ \\begin{aligned} &(2x+3)(x-4) \\\\ &\\quad {}+(2x+3)(x-6)=0. \\end{aligned} \\]",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(\\dfrac{7}{2}\\)",
    "B": "\\(4\\)",
    "C": "\\(5\\)",
    "D": "\\(7\\)",
    "E": "\\(13\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "A",
  "Solution": "Both terms contain \\(2x+3\\), so factoring out that expression reveals the roots directly:\n\\[\n\\begin{aligned}\n&(2x+3)(x-4)+(2x+3)(x-6)\\\\\n&\\qquad=(2x+3)\\bigl((x-4)+(x-6)\\bigr)\\\\\n&\\qquad=(2x+3)(2x-10).\n\\end{aligned}\n\\]\nA product is zero exactly when at least one factor is zero. Thus all the roots are given by\n\\[\n2x+3=0\\quad\\text{or}\\quad2x-10=0,\n\\]\nso \\(x=-\\frac32\\) or \\(x=5\\). Their sum is\n\\[\n-\\frac32+5=\\boxed{\\frac72},\n\\]\nchoice \\(\\boxed{\\text{A}}\\).",
